166
00:31:15,269 --> 00:31:20,399
My Bey, you stopped me once, but I
blew up Sogut this time.

167
00:31:22,082 --> 00:31:25,940
Mad man, you were supposed to blew
up only the tunnels!

168
00:31:25,940 --> 00:31:28,330
Even I nearly blew up myself, my Bey.

169
00:31:29,666 --> 00:31:31,446
Cerkutay.

170
00:31:33,712 --> 00:31:36,971
How is your hand my Bey?
Did the cure work?

171
00:31:36,971 --> 00:31:38,466
Where did you find them?

172
00:31:38,466 --> 00:31:42,976
Osman Bey commanded.
We got it from Melik's store.

173
00:31:42,976 --> 00:31:48,269
Cerkutay, is these the betrayer
Idris' remedy?

174
00:31:48,269 --> 00:31:51,699
- Yes, this is it.
- Are you serious Cerkutay?

175
00:31:54,683 --> 00:32:00,637
My Bey, your hand will recover.
You'll be Bamsı the double weapon again!

176
00:32:00,637 --> 00:32:06,987
Oh Cerkutay oh! So you're saying that
Bamsı Bey attend fights with double weapon!

177
00:32:13,434 --> 00:32:16,864
Let's apply it, Cerkutay.

178
00:32:20,452 --> 00:32:22,522
What happened Cerkutay?

179
00:32:23,248 --> 00:32:25,068
Bamsı Bey.

180
00:32:25,991 --> 00:32:29,341
You'll teach me how to use
double swords, right?

181
00:32:31,181 --> 00:32:33,001
You promised.

182
00:32:33,303 --> 00:32:39,531
Cerkutay, Cerkutay, Cerkutay,
once I heal up...

183
00:32:39,531 --> 00:32:44,071
Once I heal up, I'll teach you everything!

184
00:32:51,676 --> 00:32:54,246
My Bey, this is the first apply.

185
00:33:01,808 --> 00:33:06,576
It worked, son.
I'm recovering.

186
00:33:06,576 --> 00:33:08,916
I'll fight from now on.

187
00:33:11,916 --> 00:33:13,496
Mashallah.

188
00:33:13,923 --> 00:33:16,361
Oy Cerkutay oy.

189
00:33:16,361 --> 00:33:18,692
Oy Bamsı Bey Oy.

190
00:33:18,692 --> 00:33:21,652
- Mashallah, huh?
- Mashallah(praise be!) my Bey.

191
00:33:24,316 --> 00:33:28,236
Mashallah, Mashallah.

192
00:33:29,532 --> 00:33:31,402
It was a huge war.

193
00:33:31,565 --> 00:33:34,225
You broke the infidels.

194
00:33:34,310 --> 00:33:35,880
Mashallah.

195
00:33:37,616 --> 00:33:42,566
However, Nicola knows we joined
Osman Bey in the war.

196
00:33:43,746 --> 00:33:46,376
This is going to be rough.

197
00:33:47,452 --> 00:33:49,702
He'll want to meet me.

198
00:33:49,743 --> 00:33:53,613
We have to stop our trade
with Nicola, my Bey.

199
00:33:53,830 --> 00:33:58,550
We don't have another option to
infiltrate in the castle. Not now Malhun.

200
00:34:01,635 --> 00:34:06,205
Osman Bey is satisfied with our help,
I think.

201
00:34:07,474 --> 00:34:10,574
He invites us to dinner.

202
00:34:13,404 --> 00:34:16,793
So he wants to get closer.

203
00:34:18,344 --> 00:34:23,214
He found the betrayer in his tent.
He'll be stronger now.

204
00:34:30,257 --> 00:34:37,286
I saw him in the battlefield, father. He
was strong, he was wise.

205
00:34:41,166 --> 00:34:43,376
He saved my life.

206
00:34:46,416 --> 00:34:48,626
Okay, good.

207
00:34:52,808 --> 00:34:57,748
Muslums take care of each other
in battlefield.

208
00:35:02,148 --> 00:35:04,238
Excuse me then, my Bey.

209
00:35:09,657 --> 00:35:11,357
Malhun.

210
00:35:14,426 --> 00:35:20,326
So, what do you think of Osman Bey?

211
00:35:22,510 --> 00:35:26,990
You were used to say he was our blood,
he was Ertugrul Ghazi's son...

212
00:35:27,070 --> 00:35:30,500
before we land here.

213
00:35:31,680 --> 00:35:34,960
You were right my Bey.

214
00:35:36,815 --> 00:35:39,105
Only this?

215
00:35:41,768 --> 00:35:43,998
Isn't this enough, father?

216
00:35:49,605 --> 00:35:54,455
You can go.
Have rest, daughter.

217
00:36:09,988 --> 00:36:11,438
Bahadır!

218
00:36:16,658 --> 00:36:18,378
Yes my Bey.

219
00:36:18,630 --> 00:36:23,040
Tell me what happened in the battlefield.

220
00:36:27,412 --> 00:36:31,752
Osman Bey put us under his brother
Gündüz's order, my Bey.

221
00:36:33,829 --> 00:36:36,069
We did our job.

222
00:36:36,605 --> 00:36:40,426
Didn't Malhun say anything?

223
00:36:40,426 --> 00:36:42,266
She didn't, my Bey.

224
00:36:42,339 --> 00:36:44,579
She didn't ha?

225
00:36:45,444 --> 00:36:51,934
She got under Gündüz Bey's order
by one word of Osman Bey, ha?

226
00:37:04,166 --> 00:37:08,356
Because of you! Because of you!

227
00:37:08,447 --> 00:37:11,817
Because of you!

228
00:37:11,923 --> 00:37:16,433
I lost because of you!

229
00:37:17,577 --> 00:37:20,657
I lost because of you!

230
00:37:21,029 --> 00:37:25,879
Do you see it?
I prepared it for you.

231
00:37:29,356 --> 00:37:32,626
I am begging you, sir.
I am innocent.

232
00:37:32,965 --> 00:37:34,585
I am innocent.

233
00:37:35,625 --> 00:37:39,935
Whose fault is this if it not yours?

234
00:37:40,063 --> 00:37:42,413
Whose fault is it?

235
00:37:44,057 --> 00:37:46,217
Sir, I am innocent.

236
00:37:47,275 --> 00:37:52,405
I held you responsible for everything!

237
00:37:52,933 --> 00:37:54,993
You are the guilty one!

238
00:37:58,557 --> 00:38:03,047
- It's your fault!
- I am begging you!

239
00:38:03,763 --> 00:38:08,243
It's your fault!
I lost because of you!

240
00:38:08,939 --> 00:38:14,459
I lost because of your silliness!
Because of your silliness!

241
00:38:24,676 --> 00:38:28,696
Look!
Your grave is ready!

242
00:38:36,559 --> 00:38:40,209
Who did it if it wasn't you?

243
00:38:41,235 --> 00:38:43,964
- I am begging you sir.
- Tell me!

244
00:38:43,964 --> 00:38:48,831
I was hiding it in my castle! How did you
lost it!

245
00:38:48,831 --> 00:38:54,591
How did you lost it!
How can it be?

246
00:38:57,700 --> 00:39:00,770
No, sir. I am begging you.
Please don't kill me.

247
00:39:01,400 --> 00:39:07,700
How could you lost it!?
How could you?

248
00:39:07,995 --> 00:39:11,695
- Where is it now?
- I don't know anything.

249
00:39:12,072 --> 00:39:15,022
Please sir don't kill me.

250
00:39:15,346 --> 00:39:18,896
Whose fault is this if it is not yours?

251
00:39:19,100 --> 00:39:21,560
Who was responsible?

252
00:39:24,969 --> 00:39:28,919
Sir, sir please. I am begging you sir.

253
00:39:29,734 --> 00:39:32,024
- Osman.
- What Osman.

254
00:39:32,546 --> 00:39:36,436
He shot Dündar with an arrow
and killed him.

255
00:39:38,268 --> 00:39:40,998
It was Dündar!

256
00:39:40,998 --> 00:39:44,448
Osman learned I killed potter Idris.

257
00:39:48,477 --> 00:39:51,047
It was Dündar.

258
00:39:51,704 --> 00:39:54,904
He saw the tunnels in the map...

259
00:39:55,502 --> 00:39:58,392
when he came here.

260
00:39:58,634 --> 00:40:01,594
So he told everything to Osman
before he died.

261
00:40:02,013 --> 00:40:04,123
Osman..

262
00:40:04,123 --> 00:40:08,443
Osman's friends are increasing...

263
00:40:08,443 --> 00:40:12,443
...and his foes are diminishing.

264
00:40:16,548 --> 00:40:21,908
Send a messenger to Umur Bey.
I want to see him in my castle.

265
00:40:24,759 --> 00:40:28,759
-Get out!
-Right away, sir.

266
00:40:30,287 --> 00:40:38,647
You will pay for helping Osman!
You will! You will!

267
00:40:45,305 --> 00:40:49,305
You will pay!

268
00:41:36,629 --> 00:41:44,199
My Allah, give us halal food,
a fate without hypocrisy...

269
00:41:44,199 --> 00:41:48,799
...and faith without doubt.
-Amin.

270
00:41:48,799 --> 00:41:51,379
-Amin.
-Amin.

271
00:41:51,379 --> 00:42:00,099
Make the hearts of those who sit here
closer to those of the others.

272
00:42:00,796 --> 00:42:03,076
-Amin.
-Amin.

273
00:42:03,076 --> 00:42:07,746
And make this unity stand forever.

274
00:42:07,746 --> 00:42:09,666
-Amin.
-Amin.

275
00:42:31,876 --> 00:42:38,906
Did you get used to the tribe, Kumral
Abdal? Was Osman Bey right to invite you?

276
00:42:41,308 --> 00:42:47,068
Our hearts were in the same place,
now so are we, my sheik.

277
00:42:50,860 --> 00:42:54,860
Thank you.
Thank you.

278
00:42:55,996 --> 00:43:02,286
Now, my sheik Edebali will illuminate
Söğüt with his light.

279
00:43:02,931 --> 00:43:08,121
And Kumral Abdal's fire will burn
in our tribe.

280
00:43:08,710 --> 00:43:11,170
Not at all.

281
00:43:11,170 --> 00:43:15,170
Won't you miss the mountains,
the forests, Kumral Abdal?

282
00:43:16,310 --> 00:43:23,200
Of course, Bala Hatun. I'll be on
the ways when I do.

283
00:43:24,689 --> 00:43:31,759
We are grateful for being destined
with victory.

284
00:43:31,899 --> 00:43:37,499
Osman Bey, may your sword always
be sharp.

285
00:43:37,499 --> 00:43:41,499
Amin, my sheik. Amin.
But...

286
00:43:42,010 --> 00:43:46,010
keep praying for us.

287
00:43:47,477 --> 00:43:54,917
As you stand together against the
enemies of Islam...

288
00:43:55,236 --> 00:44:01,226
Muslims will be secured from the
dangers of the heathens.

289
00:44:04,213 --> 00:44:08,713
My sheik, don't worry.

290
00:44:08,713 --> 00:44:14,593
We drew our swords against
the enemies of the faith.

291
00:44:16,364 --> 00:44:27,544
But Osman as long as Osman Bey tells
his own commander to lead our alps...

292
00:44:28,846 --> 00:44:34,346
this will make us feel humiliated.

293
00:44:37,888 --> 00:44:44,028
Mashallah, they fought well.

294
00:44:52,948 --> 00:44:58,448
Malhun Hatun made the victory
easier.

295
00:44:59,222 --> 00:45:03,222
We did our job, Osman Bey.

296
00:45:11,314 --> 00:45:16,364
-Nikola will seek revenge now.
-Right.

297
00:45:16,875 --> 00:45:20,875
Right. But after the damage
he took...

298
00:45:20,875 --> 00:45:25,015
it won't be an easy recovery.

299
00:45:26,169 --> 00:45:30,169
We still need to be careful.

300
00:45:30,169 --> 00:45:33,299
Togay is back.

301
00:45:34,912 --> 00:45:39,372
Umur Bey, you should
be careful too.

302
00:45:39,372 --> 00:45:44,562
You can never know where and when
that snake will attack.

303
00:45:47,292 --> 00:45:51,892
Either night or morning...

304
00:45:51,892 --> 00:45:57,432
whenever he comes,
wherever he comes from...

305
00:45:57,432 --> 00:46:02,332
our alps stand ready
and eager to fight.

306
00:46:03,287 --> 00:46:09,687
-Don't worry, Osman Bey.
-Mashallah. Mashallah.

307
00:46:10,636 --> 00:46:16,776
Don't act on your own.
Tell us when something happens.

308
00:46:17,054 --> 00:46:23,244
We would love to help our brothers.

309
00:46:24,318 --> 00:46:31,078
We know, Osman Bey.
Whenever you need us, we are ready.

310
00:46:34,656 --> 00:46:38,656
Thank you.

311
00:47:00,216 --> 00:47:05,196
Villagers, merchants, shopkeepers...

312
00:47:05,196 --> 00:47:09,196
they are all migrating to Osman's
tribe!

313
00:47:10,969 --> 00:47:14,969
I should've paid the tax
to the Seljuks, Nikola!

314
00:47:16,059 --> 00:47:20,059
Enough, Yasu.

315
00:47:25,166 --> 00:47:30,106
-Have they all left?
-Some stay at Yarhisar.

316
00:47:30,215 --> 00:47:34,995
But I'm sure that they are preparing
to leave.

317
00:47:34,995 --> 00:47:39,767
I will kill them all and send their
corpses to Osman's tribe!

318
00:47:46,375 --> 00:47:50,805
Now, listen to me well, Yasu.

319
00:47:50,805 --> 00:47:55,442
You will make sure that they all
reach to Osman's tribe.

320
00:47:59,645 --> 00:48:03,915
Then, you'll place your most
trusted man...

321
00:48:03,915 --> 00:48:07,915
among them.

322
00:48:08,832 --> 00:48:12,832
That man will bring you information
from Osman.

323
00:48:12,832 --> 00:48:16,832
And you'll know where Osman is.

324
00:48:21,201 --> 00:48:27,951
And you won't come to me and
cry like a child again, Yasu.

325
00:48:33,748 --> 00:48:39,818
Now leave and do as I say.

326
00:49:27,105 --> 00:49:31,105
-What is happening here?
-We are here to see Osman Bey.

327
00:49:37,672 --> 00:49:41,672
-What's the situation?
-They want to see Osman Bey.

328
00:49:48,639 --> 00:49:54,299
-What do you want from Osman Bey?
-His justice and mercy.

329
00:50:06,791 --> 00:50:10,791
It is unbelievable! How can they take
refuge in Osman?

330
00:50:11,116 --> 00:50:14,726
This is a calamity, Nikola!

331
00:50:14,726 --> 00:50:18,906
If you lose your reputation, we'll
lose the war before it starts!

332
00:50:20,795 --> 00:50:25,355
We need the refugees back before
Osman gets stronger.

333
00:50:29,108 --> 00:50:32,838
Are you talking about
attacking the Kayı Tribe?

334
00:50:32,838 --> 00:50:37,108
Yes! I'm talking about
uprooting that tree, Nikola!

335
00:50:37,745 --> 00:50:42,445
How many soldiers do you have, Kalanos?

336
00:50:46,104 --> 00:50:50,104
To uproot a tree...

337
00:50:50,104 --> 00:50:53,124
you should be as strong as Hercules.

338
00:50:53,124 --> 00:50:57,124
We'll get soldiers from the lords and be
as strong as Hercules!

339
00:51:05,848 --> 00:51:10,318
Being like Hercules isn't enough
to beat Osman.

340
00:51:11,020 --> 00:51:15,020
We need the god of war Mars
as well.

341
00:51:26,384 --> 00:51:30,384
-May I enter, my bey?
-Come!

342
00:51:40,807 --> 00:51:43,537
Welcome.

343
00:51:46,378 --> 00:51:51,448
Be at ease. I'm listening.
Go on.

344
00:51:52,501 --> 00:51:58,411
My bey, we heard that you are
just. That's why we came.

345
00:52:05,525 --> 00:52:09,525
-What's the problem?
-We ran away from the lord of Yarhisar.

346
00:52:09,579 --> 00:52:13,579
The tax they gather for Seljuks and
Mongols is killing us.

347
00:52:21,459 --> 00:52:25,459
Don't hand us over to them, Osman Bey.

348
00:52:25,459 --> 00:52:29,109
Give us lands and we'll serve you
with loyalty.

349
00:52:29,149 --> 00:52:33,459
Not at all.
Not at all.

350
00:52:40,284 --> 00:52:46,134
Göktuğ, prepare tents for
our guests.

351
00:52:48,100 --> 00:52:51,730
-Host our guests.
-As you say, my bey.

352
00:52:51,730 --> 00:52:55,640
May God protect you, Osman Bey.
We knew that you would protect us.

353
00:52:55,640 --> 00:52:59,750
Thank you.
Thank you.

354
00:53:09,798 --> 00:53:13,798
Göktuğ, Boran.

355
00:53:16,114 --> 00:53:20,914
-Provide every need they have.
-All right, my bey.

356
00:53:21,118 --> 00:53:25,118
But keep your eyes on them.

357
00:53:26,614 --> 00:53:30,614
There might be traitors among
those poor people.

358
00:53:30,614 --> 00:53:34,614
Don't worry, my bey.
We'll be cautious.

359
00:53:37,341 --> 00:53:40,051
All right.

360
00:53:44,323 --> 00:53:48,233
Why don't we kill both of
them here?

361
00:53:48,233 --> 00:53:52,323
We need Togay for the refugees,
Kalanos.

362
00:53:52,822 --> 00:53:56,822
You will learn to be patient.

363
00:54:12,198 --> 00:54:17,638
Did you think that you'll be free of
Geyhatu's wrath by taking my sword?

364
00:54:23,047 --> 00:54:27,577
Get out. All of you.
Get out.

365
00:54:38,155 --> 00:54:42,925
What if there is more to that, Osman Bey?
Maybe it's Nikola's plan.

366
00:54:42,925 --> 00:54:49,535
While we were waiting for Nikola's next
move, this makes me think.

367
00:54:50,779 --> 00:54:54,779
But you let them settle in our tribe.

368
00:54:54,779 --> 00:54:58,779
If Nikola thinks of a new move...

369
00:54:58,779 --> 00:55:02,779
we need to use that
for our advantage.

370
00:55:03,632 --> 00:55:08,932
If we take our caution, then
we'll win.

371
00:55:08,932 --> 00:55:14,152
And we'll beat the unity
of those lords.

372
00:55:23,648 --> 00:55:28,058
Brother, think about it.

373
00:55:28,058 --> 00:55:32,908
We are showing the justice and the
toleration of the Kayı.

374
00:55:33,267 --> 00:55:39,917
We are destroying the crusader alliance!

375
00:55:42,097 --> 00:55:48,527
Then, all the non-Muslims
who complain about their lords...

376
00:55:48,527 --> 00:55:53,287
will take refuge in us.

377
00:55:53,429 --> 00:55:57,229
We will turn this to our advantage.

378
00:55:57,229 --> 00:56:03,929
But if we'll take them in, we'll
need more lands.

379
00:56:04,356 --> 00:56:09,276
Then, we'll jihad even more!

380
00:56:10,653 --> 00:56:14,653
We will, brother.
We will.

381
00:56:16,047 --> 00:56:20,047
-Together!
-Thank you.

382
00:56:26,346 --> 00:56:31,976
Do you know what I see when I look
at you, Nikola? A clumsy cat...

383
00:56:31,976 --> 00:56:37,296
who likes fish but afraid to get into
the river.

384
00:56:37,296 --> 00:56:42,046
And two-faced too.

385
00:56:42,046 --> 00:56:46,646
Traitor. You betrayed me.

386
00:56:46,646 --> 00:56:49,286
You dishonored your word.

387
00:56:57,558 --> 00:57:01,558
Camuha...

388
00:57:07,306 --> 00:57:12,316
who worked with Osman,
killed my soldiers.

389
00:57:12,316 --> 00:57:16,886
So, we are even.

390
00:57:16,886 --> 00:57:21,056
What else do you want, Togay?

391
00:57:21,056 --> 00:57:27,696
If you are here, you'll suggest an
alliance against Osman.

392
00:57:30,693 --> 00:57:37,023
I don't need an alliance against Osman.

393
00:57:38,886 --> 00:57:42,886
You do.

394
00:57:42,886 --> 00:57:46,886
He buried your dreams
in the tunnels.

395
00:57:53,479 --> 00:57:57,479
Did you give him the
fire barrells...

396
00:57:57,479 --> 00:58:01,479
to explode the tunnels?

397
00:58:02,549 --> 00:58:06,549
You couldn't even protect your
fire barrels.

398
00:58:06,549 --> 00:58:10,549
Firstly, look at your friends
that you trade with.

399
00:58:11,705 --> 00:58:16,635
Togay, what do you want?

400
00:58:17,112 --> 00:58:21,112
You and the lord of Yarhisar...

401
00:58:21,112 --> 00:58:25,112
must've received your gifts.

402
00:58:25,967 --> 00:58:29,967
-This is Yaso's coltan.
-Is this Osman's work?

403
00:58:29,967 --> 00:58:33,817
It's Togay's.

404
00:58:33,817 --> 00:58:38,737
You will convince the lords
to pay their taxes.

405
00:58:38,737 --> 00:58:42,737
Otherwise, you know what happens.

406
00:58:42,737 --> 00:58:46,737
The people of Yarhisar took refuge
in Osman, Togay.

407
00:58:46,737 --> 00:58:52,347
-What does that mean?
-Farmers, merchants, shopkeepers...

408
00:58:52,347 --> 00:59:00,077
everyone who pays taxes for Geyhatu
takes refuge in Osman.

409
00:59:01,036 --> 00:59:06,576
So, there is no better time to
make an alliance.

410
00:59:07,709 --> 00:59:13,669
Bring the refugees and take
the taxes.

411
00:59:14,257 --> 00:59:16,867
Or...

412
00:59:19,560 --> 00:59:23,560
Or we can do this.

413
00:59:23,560 --> 00:59:27,560
You and I can fight.

414
00:59:27,560 --> 00:59:31,560
Then, you can see if I'm a
clumsy cat...

415
00:59:31,560 --> 00:59:35,560
or a bloody lion.

416
00:59:38,132 --> 00:59:43,447
Only Osman can benefit from
our fight, Togay.

417
00:59:43,447 --> 00:59:48,137
But if we unite for a final blow...

418
00:59:48,137 --> 00:59:52,137
we both can benefit.

419
00:59:54,308 --> 00:59:58,308
I will take the refugees from Osman.

420
00:59:58,984 --> 01:00:03,744
And the lord of Yarhisar will pay taxes.

421
01:00:03,744 --> 01:00:09,784
And Osman will die.

422
01:00:10,166 --> 01:00:13,796
It's simple.

423
01:00:38,195 --> 01:00:43,855
-Will we trust these barbarians?
-For now, Kalanos.

424
01:00:43,893 --> 01:00:48,533
For now, we need each other.

425
01:00:48,592 --> 01:00:52,132
What about later?

426
01:01:01,815 --> 01:01:06,345
Will Nikola keep his word
after getting the refugees?

427
01:01:06,345 --> 01:01:11,805
He will keep it as long as he needs our
warriors. We need his soldiers too.

428
01:01:11,831 --> 01:01:15,981
Go to Osman. Ask for the refugees.

429
01:01:15,987 --> 01:01:19,987
-What if he refuses?
-If he does...

430
01:01:19,987 --> 01:01:23,987
he knows that I will be with
Nikola.

431
01:01:23,987 --> 01:01:28,917
If he doesn't work with me,
he will pay for it.

432
01:01:36,641 --> 01:01:41,091
You are our guests at our tribe until
we find you a place.

433
01:01:41,091 --> 01:01:46,201
Feel like home.

434
01:01:46,469 --> 01:01:50,149
Come to me if you need anything.

435
01:01:50,149 --> 01:01:53,869
May God protect Osman Bey's
compassionate wife.

436
01:01:58,717 --> 01:02:02,717
-I brought apples!
-Bring it.

437
01:02:04,324 --> 01:02:07,854
-Thank you.
-Enjoy it.

438
01:02:07,854 --> 01:02:11,854
Here it is.
You too.

439
01:02:19,655 --> 01:02:23,655
It's hard to leave your home, alps.

440
01:02:26,390 --> 01:02:31,620
They are poor. We need to make
them feel good.

441
01:02:34,120 --> 01:02:40,010
They are sent to us by Allah.

442
01:02:41,137 --> 01:02:47,217
Don't worry, Kumral Abdal.
We'll protect them.

443
01:02:47,760 --> 01:02:51,760
We'll help them with Allah's help.

444
01:02:51,760 --> 01:02:56,860
We won't separate them from the Muslims.

445
01:02:56,860 --> 01:03:00,860
We'll show them the beauty of our
laws and our religion.

446
01:03:01,370 --> 01:03:05,170
May Allah bless you.

447
01:03:06,713 --> 01:03:10,713
May Allah bless us all, Kumral Abdal.

448
01:03:17,811 --> 01:03:22,531
Come here, come here.
Come here.

449
01:03:38,469 --> 01:03:41,589
Mashallah.

450
01:03:47,452 --> 01:03:50,682
Come on now.

451
01:03:50,682 --> 01:03:55,852
-Alps!
-May God protect you, Osman Bey.

452
01:03:58,849 --> 01:04:03,769
Not at all. Not at all

453
01:04:04,534 --> 01:04:08,534
May God protect you, Osman Bey.

454
01:04:10,430 --> 01:04:16,400
You trusted our justice and gathered
under our flag.

455
01:04:16,562 --> 01:04:21,802
Now, now you are in security.

456
01:04:21,802 --> 01:04:25,802
Until you are given lands...

457
01:04:25,802 --> 01:04:29,784
you are my responsibility.

458
01:04:29,784 --> 01:04:35,364
We don't discriminate among the
people.

459
01:04:36,091 --> 01:04:42,151
In my lands, the security of your
religion...

460
01:04:42,151 --> 01:04:47,362
food and dignity is secured
by...

461
01:04:48,105 --> 01:04:54,485
Ertuğrul Ghazi's son Osman Bey.

462
01:04:55,094 --> 01:04:59,094
May God protect you Osman Bey.

463
01:05:02,919 --> 01:05:06,919
Thank you.
Thank you.

464
01:05:12,588 --> 01:05:16,588
Brother, let's go Söğüt.

465
01:05:18,932 --> 01:05:23,332
Osman Bey. We have another guest.

466
01:05:30,814 --> 01:05:34,814
I came here as the messenger
of the Ilkhaganete.

467
01:05:34,814 --> 01:05:39,634
I'm unarmed.
I have things to say.

468
01:05:40,021 --> 01:05:44,021
We searched him. He is clean.

469
01:05:47,225 --> 01:05:52,205
Take him to my tent.
Inform Bamsı Bey.

470
01:05:52,205 --> 01:05:54,885
-As you order, my bey.
-As you order, my bey.

471
01:06:27,001 --> 01:06:31,001
Won't you get down from your
throne...

472
01:06:31,001 --> 01:06:35,001
and welcome your friend...

473
01:06:35,311 --> 01:06:39,751
Tekfur Nikola?
-What are you planning Umur Bey?

474
01:06:40,472 --> 01:06:46,422
First, you came here and talked about
friendship then you gave your men to Osman.

475
01:06:47,328 --> 01:06:51,678
Tell me, what are you planning?

476
01:06:53,941 --> 01:06:59,891
What's this anger, Nikola?
Welcome me first.

477
01:06:59,891 --> 01:07:03,391
What are you planning?

478
01:07:07,629 --> 01:07:12,425
Somehow, Osman Bey took
my daughter...

479
01:07:12,425 --> 01:07:17,455
Malhun's mind away.

480
01:07:17,455 --> 01:07:23,285
Maybe he took his heart as well, Umur Bey.

481
01:07:28,763 --> 01:07:33,933
She took her alps and went
to Osman without telling me.

482
01:07:34,510 --> 01:07:38,510
I wouldn't allow it if I knew it.

483
01:07:38,510 --> 01:07:42,510
Trust me, trade with you is more
important than anything.

484
01:07:43,201 --> 01:07:48,591
Without trade, what's the point
of staying here?

485
01:07:59,408 --> 01:08:04,038
From Kızılbeyoğulları, Umur...

486
01:08:05,622 --> 01:08:08,342
Bey.

487
01:08:08,342 --> 01:08:13,342
How will I know that you and
Osman aren't playing together?

488
01:08:13,391 --> 01:08:18,301
If you had thought that...

489
01:08:18,301 --> 01:08:22,791
you would've beheaded me.

490
01:08:26,765 --> 01:08:32,515
How do you know that I won't
behead you now?

491
01:08:32,515 --> 01:08:38,415
You need me as much as I need you...

492
01:08:38,761 --> 01:08:45,082
Nikola. That's why we are allied.

493
01:08:46,555 --> 01:08:53,066
Osman can offer you what I offer you...

494
01:08:53,926 --> 01:08:58,553
Umur Bey.
-I want trade.

495
01:08:58,553 --> 01:09:02,524
And trade comes from İnegöl...

496
01:09:02,524 --> 01:09:07,823
İznik, Bursa and even Constantinople.

497
01:09:08,014 --> 01:09:12,014
I want to grow.

498
01:09:13,256 --> 01:09:17,256
Come on, Nikola.

499
01:09:17,256 --> 01:09:21,256
Smile to your friend.

500
01:10:28,433 --> 01:10:30,403
Osman Bey.

501
01:10:43,206 --> 01:10:49,266
The last time I heard, you were slaughtering
the Byzantines running away from me.

502
01:10:49,266 --> 01:10:55,646
What is it? Did Togay send you to
show goodness?

503
01:10:59,062 --> 01:11:05,412
We heard that Tengry sent you unexpected
guests from Yarhisar, Osman Bey.

504
01:11:06,932 --> 01:11:10,932
They took refuge in you.

505
01:11:12,301 --> 01:11:17,471
They did it without asking us.

506
01:11:17,471 --> 01:11:22,561
And you accepted them without
asking us.

507
01:11:37,470 --> 01:11:42,590
You washed the whole world with
blood...

508
01:11:42,590 --> 01:11:47,540
You even dare to step over Genghis Khan,
huh?

509
01:11:48,349 --> 01:11:52,349
Didn't Genghis Khan said that Tengry's
unexpected guests can't be touched...

510
01:11:52,349 --> 01:11:56,349
just as my ancestor Oghuz Khan said?

511
01:11:57,327 --> 01:12:01,327
Tell me!

512
01:12:01,327 --> 01:12:05,327
Did someone step on that Dark Shaman
Togay's tail?

513
01:12:06,682 --> 01:12:12,732
Don't speak Genghis Khan's name,
Osman Bey!

514
01:12:12,732 --> 01:12:16,732
Osman Bey.

515
01:12:18,108 --> 01:12:22,108
Bamsı Bey, hold on.

516
01:12:35,787 --> 01:12:39,787
I will remind Togay the words
of Genghis Khan.

517
01:12:39,787 --> 01:12:45,177
''Don't touch Turks as long as
they don't touch you.''

518
01:12:46,680 --> 01:12:51,210
If you target those who take
refuge in me...

519
01:12:51,210 --> 01:12:55,210
I will take his eyes out...

520
01:12:55,210 --> 01:12:59,210
before beheading him.

521
01:13:00,522 --> 01:13:06,982
If you don't give us the refugees...

522
01:13:06,982 --> 01:13:13,662
we'll raze your tribe, Osman Bey.

523
01:13:27,629 --> 01:13:33,319
He knows that he can't beat me...

524
01:13:33,319 --> 01:13:38,399
now he wants to tyrannize
those poor people.

525
01:13:38,399 --> 01:13:44,839
What is it? Do you want to ally
Nikola who you have betrayed?

526
01:13:45,753 --> 01:13:50,073
Are you after the gold that goes
to the Ilkhaganete treasury?

527
01:13:51,162 --> 01:13:54,112
Tell me!

528
01:13:56,809 --> 01:14:00,809
Kayı Tribe is a lion's den.

529
01:14:00,809 --> 01:14:06,449
Weasels like you have no chance.
Just dare to come.

530
01:14:07,105 --> 01:14:11,845
Then, we'll drown you in
your blood.

531
01:14:14,570 --> 01:14:20,530
So, you want us to bad to attack you?

532
01:14:21,676 --> 01:14:26,026
You will get what you want, Osman Bey.

533
01:14:33,551 --> 01:14:36,791
Bamsı Bey.

534
01:14:37,065 --> 01:14:41,065
You had things to say to Camuha.

535
01:14:41,065 --> 01:14:46,675
I do, Osman Bey. I do.
I'll send my regards to Togay.

536
01:14:48,457 --> 01:14:53,987
And I will tell him...

537
01:14:57,192 --> 01:15:02,882
The revenge of Abdurrahman Ghazi
will be taken.

538
01:15:15,139 --> 01:15:19,139
Now, take this weasel away.

539
01:15:28,587 --> 01:15:34,527
We'll avenge Abdurrahman Ghazi,
Bamsı Bey. Don't you worry.

540
01:15:34,527 --> 01:15:38,527
I know, Osman Bey.
Thank Allah.

541
01:15:51,802 --> 01:15:54,492
My beys.

542
01:15:55,474 --> 01:16:00,974
-Tell me what you think.
-It's about taxes, it seems.

543
01:16:00,974 --> 01:16:04,974
Geyhatu is after the taxes.

544
01:16:04,974 --> 01:16:09,434
We can stop Togay, of course.
But if Geyhatu himself comes...

545
01:16:09,434 --> 01:16:13,434
No, Geyhatu is busy.

546
01:16:13,434 --> 01:16:17,434
He can't come here among
all the trouble he has.

547
01:16:17,434 --> 01:16:24,244
-He left it for Togay.
-Those who come won't leave alive.

548
01:16:25,496 --> 01:16:30,926
They won't dare to attack when
the Kayı alps are here.

549
01:16:32,369 --> 01:16:37,609
When did Muslims hand over their
refugees?

550
01:16:39,747 --> 01:16:45,177
He'll do everything to get the taxes.

551
01:16:45,177 --> 01:16:50,447
He'll even ally with Nikola.

552
01:16:50,447 --> 01:16:55,787
If needed, he'll attack our tribe.

553
01:16:57,872 --> 01:17:02,192
But we won't hand over our refugees.

554
01:17:02,453 --> 01:17:07,393
And we won't bow down to this threat.

555
01:17:08,715 --> 01:17:13,305
Brother, prepare for war.

556
01:17:13,305 --> 01:17:17,200
-All right.
-It's time for Togay to learn...

557
01:17:17,200 --> 01:17:23,730
what happens to those who
touch the Turks.

558
01:17:31,516 --> 01:17:37,586
Osman won't give the refugees.
I failed to convince him.

559
01:17:38,500 --> 01:17:42,500
He will. Either with his hands...

560
01:17:42,500 --> 01:17:46,500
in peace as morning winds...

561
01:17:46,500 --> 01:17:51,820
or without his will, with no mercy.

562
01:17:53,422 --> 01:17:59,292
Ready my horse.
The donkey that carries us all the time...

563
01:17:59,292 --> 01:18:03,292
is better than the horse that is ready
to kick us, Camuha.

564
01:18:03,292 --> 01:18:05,902
Nikola will be happy to see us.

565
01:18:09,478 --> 01:18:12,958
I'm sure of that.

566
01:18:15,367 --> 01:18:19,367
Nikola seems convinced.

567
01:18:19,997 --> 01:18:23,997
But we need to be more careful.

568
01:18:23,997 --> 01:18:29,837
We need to be cautious about supporting
Osman Bey from open.

569
01:18:31,292 --> 01:18:34,872
-What do you want us to do, father?
-For a while...

570
01:18:34,872 --> 01:18:38,332
we shouldn't be seen around.

571
01:18:38,332 --> 01:18:45,012
Otherwise, both our trade and our plans
for İnegöl will fail.

572
01:18:49,383 --> 01:18:54,543
We'll stay back from jihad to infiltrate
İnegöl.

573
01:18:57,356 --> 01:19:01,696
Isn't this the real jihad?

574
01:19:01,696 --> 01:19:06,616
Isn't it the real jihad to get into the
enemy's heart and finishing it for good?

575
01:19:08,536 --> 01:19:12,536
You know it better, father.

576
01:19:14,398 --> 01:19:18,398
Something is off with you.

577
01:19:18,398 --> 01:19:23,968
-What is it, father?
-You wouldn't question my orders before.

578
01:19:25,082 --> 01:19:29,682
I wasn't doing my job well then.

579
01:19:31,180 --> 01:19:35,180
My job isn't to undermine you.

580
01:19:35,180 --> 01:19:40,320
Those who say yes to every order are the
ones who undermine you.

581
01:19:43,611 --> 01:19:48,441
Do you know what I'm most proud of?

582
01:19:49,496 --> 01:19:53,496
That I raised you to be like this.

583
01:20:08,566 --> 01:20:13,206
My bey, the lords sent soldiers to Nikola.

584
01:20:14,314 --> 01:20:20,334
Nikola is preparing for an attack
to get the refugees back.

585
01:20:21,425 --> 01:20:25,665
We need to stop them from
supporting each other.

586
01:20:27,640 --> 01:20:33,650
We can't stop them before crushing
the snake's head.

587
01:20:34,965 --> 01:20:38,965
Call Süleyman and Melik.

588
01:21:19,814 --> 01:21:23,814
What are you doing here?
Come on!

589
01:22:09,391 --> 01:22:14,841
You will take this letter to the Pope.

590
01:22:23,066 --> 01:22:27,066
So, you are releasing us, Osman Bey?

591
01:22:36,266 --> 01:22:41,666
You know that I keep my words, Petros.

592
01:22:42,394 --> 01:22:46,394
As much as I trust the Pope's words.

593
01:22:47,220 --> 01:22:49,690
But...

594
01:22:51,351 --> 01:22:57,231
there is one last job that I want
Melik to do.

595
01:22:57,643 --> 01:23:00,183
What is it?

596
01:23:01,077 --> 01:23:05,077
You will go to İnegöl.

597
01:23:05,077 --> 01:23:09,077
You will find out how many soldiers
have the lords sent to Nikola.

598
01:23:09,077 --> 01:23:13,077
And when they will attack.

599
01:23:16,171 --> 01:23:21,021
-Then, this captivity will end, is that so?
-It will.

600
01:23:21,491 --> 01:23:25,491
It will be your redemption.

601
01:23:25,491 --> 01:23:30,091
What if Nikola find it out and kills me?

602
01:23:30,474 --> 01:23:34,474
Then I will send your heads...

603
01:23:34,474 --> 01:23:38,474
with this letter...

604
01:23:38,474 --> 01:23:41,304
and send them to the Pope.

605
01:23:57,522 --> 01:24:01,292
Now leave.

606
01:24:10,173 --> 01:24:14,173
Simon, when the battle ends...

607
01:24:14,173 --> 01:24:18,173
if your intelligence proves to be true...

608
01:24:18,173 --> 01:24:23,903
then, my alps will take you to Cunda.

609
01:24:27,910 --> 01:24:31,910
You will take a boat there.

610
01:24:38,100 --> 01:24:42,890
-Boran. Take them to their tents.
-Yes, my bey.

611
01:24:43,630 --> 01:24:46,540
As you order, my bey.

612
01:25:17,484 --> 01:25:21,484
Did Osman accept the offer?

613
01:25:22,047 --> 01:25:24,607
No.

614
01:25:24,607 --> 01:25:28,607
I didn't expect anything else.

615
01:25:28,820 --> 01:25:34,850
This is the time to unite our forces for
one last time with no treason.

616
01:25:35,081 --> 01:25:39,081
I don't need the Byzantine armies...

617
01:25:39,081 --> 01:25:43,081
for the sun to warm the earth.

618
01:25:43,430 --> 01:25:48,310
In my absence, you rolled dices and lost.

619
01:25:48,310 --> 01:25:53,200
Now you will obey my power.

620
01:25:54,410 --> 01:26:00,159
If your victory will be mine,
you will listen to every word...

621
01:26:00,159 --> 01:26:05,389
Togay the Dark Shaman speaks of.

622
01:26:14,980 --> 01:26:20,180
Nikola will come with great numbers.

623
01:26:20,681 --> 01:26:24,681
What about Togay?

624
01:26:24,681 --> 01:26:29,341
Togay will support Nikola.

625
01:26:29,843 --> 01:26:33,993
I mean, they will attack together.

626
01:26:33,993 --> 01:26:39,103
-When will they attack?
-Two days later.

627
01:26:43,320 --> 01:26:47,320
I want more information.

628
01:26:51,030 --> 01:26:55,930
You will go to İnegöl and learn
everything you can learn.

629
01:26:57,495 --> 01:27:01,495
You know that I keep my words.

630
01:27:08,672 --> 01:27:10,902
Alps.

631
01:27:22,587 --> 01:27:25,037
My beys.

632
01:27:28,797 --> 01:27:32,287
You heard everything.

633
01:27:32,718 --> 01:27:36,718
Now, tell me what you think.

634
01:27:37,384 --> 01:27:43,834
We can beat both the heathen Nikola
and the heathen Togay.

635
01:27:44,124 --> 01:27:48,124
Thank Allah.
But...

636
01:27:48,296 --> 01:27:52,296
Osman Bey, we will have many martyrs.

637
01:27:55,664 --> 01:28:00,884
We'll have many martyrs, Bamsı Bey.
But if the two armies come together...

638
01:28:00,884 --> 01:28:04,704
the victory won't be easy at all.

639
01:28:04,704 --> 01:28:09,804
We'll either set a trap,
divide them...

640
01:28:10,318 --> 01:28:14,918
or we'll face an honorable death.

641
01:28:17,790 --> 01:28:22,690
Savcı Bey talks about an honorable death.
Is this needed, Osman Bey?

642
01:28:24,399 --> 01:28:27,949
Should we knowingly face death?

643
01:28:27,949 --> 01:28:31,659
What else should we do?
Give up on our honor?

644
01:28:31,659 --> 01:28:35,659
Should we give up on the future
of the Kayı, Davud Bey?

645
01:28:37,496 --> 01:28:44,046
Will the Kayıs give up on their lives
to protect the refugees?

646
01:28:53,028 --> 01:28:57,028
Losing our honor...

647
01:28:58,739 --> 01:29:03,129
or losing our life, is that so?

648
01:29:03,129 --> 01:29:08,119
Does a nation without honor
deserve to live? Tell me!

649
01:29:08,713 --> 01:29:14,253
Who can live without laws?
Can they survive?

650
01:29:17,030 --> 01:29:22,660
Even if my all sides get surrounded,
I will still fight.

651
01:29:22,660 --> 01:29:25,720
Because I'm free.

652
01:29:37,607 --> 01:29:43,267
As the battle gets greater,
so will the victory.

653
01:29:44,215 --> 01:29:47,515
Thank you, Osman Bey.

654
01:29:48,246 --> 01:29:53,376
Now, the matter is closed.

655
01:30:01,209 --> 01:30:06,859
Brother, prepare all the alps according
to what Melik said.

656
01:30:06,859 --> 01:30:11,409
-We will fight.
-As you order, Osman Bey.

657
01:30:17,152 --> 01:30:21,142
-Thank you, Osman Bey.
-Bamsı Bey.

658
01:30:31,737 --> 01:30:35,197
Bamsı Bey.

659
01:30:37,162 --> 01:30:39,942
How is your hand?

660
01:30:43,263 --> 01:30:49,373
The cure. The cure works, Osman Bey.
It gets better every day.

661
01:30:51,547 --> 01:30:55,547
I'll be on the frontline, Osman Bey.

662
01:30:55,547 --> 01:30:58,497
Not now.

663
01:30:59,772 --> 01:31:03,292
Not now, Bamsı Bey.

664
01:31:04,692 --> 01:31:08,692
You are my castle.
The post of our tribe.

665
01:31:09,569 --> 01:31:13,999
-I can't afford to lose you.
-Osman Bey...

666
01:31:15,195 --> 01:31:21,685
I fought without this hand.
Why are you saying this now?

667
01:31:22,282 --> 01:31:28,662
Camuha talks about attacking the tribe.
He might do mischief in our absence.

668
01:31:32,605 --> 01:31:35,915
For this reason...

669
01:31:39,088 --> 01:31:42,518
I will leave the tribe to you.

670
01:31:50,837 --> 01:31:54,837
If it's the order of the bey...

671
01:31:55,035 --> 01:31:58,305
I will follow, of course.

672
01:32:00,083 --> 01:32:02,553
All right, Osman Bey.

673
01:32:32,666 --> 01:32:34,116
Nikola.

674
01:32:35,084 --> 01:32:36,924
A clever devil.

675
01:32:37,724 --> 01:32:42,644
I won't survive that castle, Petros.

676
01:32:54,290 --> 01:32:58,290
-Simon...
-I don't mind dying.

677
01:32:58,290 --> 01:33:03,340
I'm ready to stake my life...

678
01:33:03,340 --> 01:33:07,340
for you to leave this tribe alive.

679
01:33:07,471 --> 01:33:13,951
But promise me, Petros.
Finish our mission.

680
01:33:14,707 --> 01:33:19,227
Kill Osman.

681
01:33:20,090 --> 01:33:24,760
May God be with you...

682
01:33:24,760 --> 01:33:28,760
and vengeance be with me.

683
01:34:16,455 --> 01:34:18,975
Bala.

684
01:34:20,762 --> 01:34:23,822
Come here.

685
01:34:27,687 --> 01:34:29,957
Come.

686
01:34:44,283 --> 01:34:48,283
My sunlight.
Are you all right?

687
01:34:48,965 --> 01:34:54,875
I am, Osman. What can trouble me
when you are here.

688
01:34:57,334 --> 01:35:01,334
Thank you. What did you do?

689
01:35:01,334 --> 01:35:04,894
Have you taken care of our guests?

690
01:35:04,894 --> 01:35:10,724
We provided all their needs, my bey.
They are praying for you in their faiths.

691
01:35:10,724 --> 01:35:14,724
May they live long.

692
01:35:14,724 --> 01:35:18,724
It's important for them to feel good.

693
01:35:19,939 --> 01:35:24,119
It's more important than anything
that the Kayı Tribe...

694
01:35:24,119 --> 01:35:28,404
should become a home for all
the oppressed people.

695
01:35:30,709 --> 01:35:34,709
The enemy wants them back.

696
01:35:34,980 --> 01:35:38,980
They want to stop the oppressed from
taking refuge in you.

697
01:35:38,980 --> 01:35:44,220
If we are a good host, we'll have
a lot more guests.

698
01:35:44,352 --> 01:35:49,232
If they feel good, they will
stay here permanently.

699
01:35:52,729 --> 01:35:57,599
If the Kayı Tribe will found a state
one day...

700
01:35:59,017 --> 01:36:03,017
it will need a lots of people.

701
01:36:09,248 --> 01:36:13,248
This is a turnout, Bala.

702
01:36:13,248 --> 01:36:17,968
We won't give our guests to
the enemy.

703
01:36:19,485 --> 01:36:25,805
Everyone will say that the Kayı
is the hope of the poor people.

704
01:36:27,567 --> 01:36:33,667
And everyone will gather
under our flag.

705
01:36:36,548 --> 01:36:40,548
Take care of the heathens, Osman Bey.

706
01:36:40,548 --> 01:36:44,548
Leave the hosting to me.

707
01:36:44,548 --> 01:36:47,548
Be at ease.

708
01:38:14,051 --> 01:38:17,561
This belonged to my mother.

709
01:38:20,801 --> 01:38:24,801
Be at ease.

710
01:38:35,701 --> 01:38:39,681
I understand. I understand.
I understand, Simon.

711
01:38:39,681 --> 01:38:44,091
The tunnels collapsed and you couldn't
reach Helen. Is that so?

712
01:38:44,091 --> 01:38:48,901
Yes. Everything happened so suddenly,
Nikola.

713
01:38:49,655 --> 01:38:54,645
So, Simon. How did Osman hear
about the tunnels?

714
01:38:55,872 --> 01:39:00,272
Dündar. He must've heard it
from Dündar.

715
01:39:01,020 --> 01:39:07,200
So, why didn't we hear that Dündar
got captured.

716
01:39:08,009 --> 01:39:13,509
Because Dündar got caught just
before the attack.

717
01:39:13,509 --> 01:39:18,189
And I didn't have the chance to
inform you, Nikola.

718
01:39:19,914 --> 01:39:23,204
I understand.

719
01:39:28,193 --> 01:39:32,193
I understand.
So, Simon....

720
01:39:33,782 --> 01:39:37,782
forgive my curiosity.

721
01:39:38,547 --> 01:39:42,767
One of those tunnels led to your
shop.

722
01:39:44,089 --> 01:39:48,089
How did you not get caught?

723
01:39:48,089 --> 01:39:54,459
Petros and I did everything
we can to convince Osman.

724
01:39:54,809 --> 01:39:59,289
Of course, we aren't free of suspicion.

725
01:39:59,289 --> 01:40:04,019
But Osman trusts us for now.

726
01:40:06,506 --> 01:40:11,196
So, you convinced Osman, huh?

727
01:40:11,779 --> 01:40:16,919
Yes. But Osman shouldn't
get away with it.

728
01:40:16,919 --> 01:40:22,249
We should attack Osman without
waiting for a moment.

729
01:40:22,768 --> 01:40:28,398
We should determine the time
and act accordingly, Nikola.

730
01:40:29,261 --> 01:40:32,601
Of course, Simon.

731
01:40:35,251 --> 01:40:39,251
Of course.

732
01:40:39,251 --> 01:40:43,881
I will attack Osman's tribe suddenly
with the soldiers I get from the lords.

733
01:40:45,304 --> 01:40:48,374
When?

734
01:40:50,604 --> 01:40:53,564
Very soon.

735
01:40:56,207 --> 01:41:00,207
But something in my mind...

736
01:41:00,634 --> 01:41:05,514
Simon, I was thinking...

737
01:41:05,514 --> 01:41:10,504
It must be hard to convince Osman.

738
01:41:12,448 --> 01:41:17,328
What is it, Nikola?
Don't you trust us anymore?

739
01:41:17,781 --> 01:41:21,221
Answer this.

740
01:41:21,221 --> 01:41:26,591
I want to think that we still
are friends.

741
01:41:26,821 --> 01:41:31,281
Of course, Simon.
Of course.

742
01:41:33,649 --> 01:41:36,039
Dimos.

743
01:41:58,257 --> 01:42:02,817
I saw him at the tribe.
There was someone else with him.

744
01:42:03,240 --> 01:42:07,240
They were both captives
of Osman.

745
01:42:09,263 --> 01:42:13,523
Who are you?
You are lying!

746
01:42:15,552 --> 01:42:19,552
Nikola, you must believe me!

747
01:42:19,552 --> 01:42:22,112
We aren't working for Osman!

748
01:42:22,112 --> 01:42:27,272
Simon, where is Petros?

749
01:42:30,467 --> 01:42:34,467
Have they captured him?

750
01:42:34,467 --> 01:42:40,207
And they sent you to learn what
move will I make.

751
01:42:41,017 --> 01:42:47,617
-Is that so?
-Nikola, we gave you many opportunities!

752
01:42:47,891 --> 01:42:51,891
But you failed every time.

753
01:42:51,891 --> 01:42:55,891
You slipped him away many times.

754
01:42:56,485 --> 01:43:02,455
Now, do you want to make us
pay for your mistakes?

755
01:43:02,907 --> 01:43:07,747
Simon, I'm asking for the last time.

756
01:43:07,747 --> 01:43:11,357
Where is Petros.

757
01:43:11,357 --> 01:43:15,747
I will tell him to come.

758
01:43:15,747 --> 01:43:21,577
But if you act like this, you
won't get our support anymore.

759
01:43:36,695 --> 01:43:40,695
What happened, Simon?

760
01:43:44,619 --> 01:43:48,069
What happened, Simon?

761
01:44:04,544 --> 01:44:10,194
Have your holy pope, your God
left you?

762
01:44:13,010 --> 01:44:17,800
What happened, Simon?
Tell me!

763
01:44:23,346 --> 01:44:27,346
Go to hell, Nikola!

764
01:44:45,729 --> 01:44:50,059
Every place free of the pope's
rats is a heaven for me.

765
01:44:51,125 --> 01:44:53,805
Close it.

766
01:45:07,832 --> 01:45:12,622
Now, listen to me well.
Return to the tribe.

767
01:45:12,622 --> 01:45:19,352
Tell me everything that happens
in the tribe.

768
01:45:19,641 --> 01:45:24,571
Understand?
Understand?

769
01:45:24,571 --> 01:45:26,911
Good.

770
01:45:33,729 --> 01:45:36,709
Kalanos...

771
01:45:40,168 --> 01:45:44,168
Osman knows that we'll attack.

772
01:45:47,113 --> 01:45:51,993
He knows. He knows, Kalanos.

773
01:45:51,993 --> 01:45:55,443
Osman is all alone.

774
01:45:55,443 --> 01:45:59,693
He has no one else but his alps
in his tribe.

775
01:46:01,403 --> 01:46:05,403
It's time to finish this.

776
01:46:16,108 --> 01:46:22,448
If it's as you say, a battle between
Nikola and Osman is soon.

777
01:46:23,270 --> 01:46:29,270
It will be as you say, my bey.
There will be a great battle between them.

778
01:46:29,270 --> 01:46:33,900
Nikola wants the refugees and Osman Bey
refuses.

779
01:46:33,900 --> 01:46:37,900
They will unite with Togay
and attack.

780
01:46:40,357 --> 01:46:44,737
We'll be with Osman Bey in
this honorable cause.

781
01:46:47,045 --> 01:46:51,045
No.

782
01:46:51,045 --> 01:46:57,965
No? Will we leave a bey who fights
for his tribe's honor alone?

783
01:46:59,736 --> 01:47:03,066
Bahadır.

784
01:47:08,776 --> 01:47:12,776
How many times do I have to tell you?

785
01:47:12,776 --> 01:47:16,776
I have to be seen like I'm in
peace with Nikola. That's my plan.

786
01:47:16,776 --> 01:47:22,156
This isn't a game, father.
The Kayı tribe needs help.

787
01:47:22,156 --> 01:47:26,916
If we don't help now, there might not
be a tribe left there.

788
01:47:27,611 --> 01:47:31,991
Osman Bey will take care of himself.

789
01:47:32,506 --> 01:47:36,786
We will play our own plans.

790
01:47:37,872 --> 01:47:42,762
Osman Bey will take care of himself
against both...

791
01:47:42,762 --> 01:47:46,762
Nikola and Togay, is that so?

792
01:47:46,762 --> 01:47:49,482
Yes.

793
01:47:50,423 --> 01:47:54,153
My decision is final.

794
01:48:02,956 --> 01:48:08,726
Are you thinking about the Kayı Tribe?

795
01:48:12,350 --> 01:48:16,350
I'm thinking about you, my bey.

796
01:48:16,350 --> 01:48:22,140
Your reputation.
If you allow me.

797
01:48:38,151 --> 01:48:42,151
Why am I mad at her?

798
01:48:42,151 --> 01:48:45,691
I caused this.

799
01:49:26,916 --> 01:49:30,916
Bayhoca.

800
01:49:32,273 --> 01:49:37,173
My dear son.
I still carry your smell in my heart.

801
01:49:37,173 --> 01:49:41,173
I still carry your voice
in my ears.

802
01:49:41,173 --> 01:49:47,723
You left and you won't return, I know.
But I'm still waiting.

803
01:49:54,071 --> 01:49:58,071
I see you in my dreams every night.

804
01:49:59,894 --> 01:50:03,894
I get afraid to wake up.

805
01:50:03,894 --> 01:50:10,074
I don't want to wake up.
Yesterday, you were in my dream again.

806
01:50:10,074 --> 01:50:16,634
I hugged you tightly.
To not let you go again.

807
01:50:16,985 --> 01:50:20,985
My dear son.

808
01:50:20,985 --> 01:50:23,685
Lena.

809
01:50:29,529 --> 01:50:33,529
Lena, what are you doing here?

810
01:50:34,283 --> 01:50:39,433
I'm talking to our son, Savcı.

811
01:50:41,774 --> 01:50:45,774
I'm watering his good soil.

812
01:50:46,500 --> 01:50:51,070
Savcı, is this our son laying here?

813
01:50:58,512 --> 01:51:04,322
You know that it is the body
that lays here.

814
01:51:07,373 --> 01:51:11,373
The spirit is in heaven.

815
01:51:11,496 --> 01:51:15,496
In heaven, of course.

816
01:51:16,720 --> 01:51:20,720
He is waiting for us, right?

817
01:51:21,279 --> 01:51:26,739
When the time comes, we'll go as well.

818
01:51:28,185 --> 01:51:32,985
We'll be united.
We will hug our son.

819
01:51:34,578 --> 01:51:37,888
When the time comes.

820
01:51:38,036 --> 01:51:44,636
I ask Allah to take my life before yours.

821
01:51:45,514 --> 01:51:47,414
Lena.

822
01:51:49,432 --> 01:51:54,302
-What are you saying?
-I can't live without you.

823
01:51:59,242 --> 01:52:02,862
Oh, my suffering angel.

824
01:52:03,190 --> 01:52:10,470
Would I leave you before your wiping
your tears away?

825
01:52:10,983 --> 01:52:14,453
Don't leave.

826
01:52:14,697 --> 01:52:17,917
Don't leave, Savcı.

827
01:52:18,192 --> 01:52:22,622
Don't leave me all alone.

828
01:52:25,385 --> 01:52:28,805
I can't bear it.

829
01:52:29,516 --> 01:52:32,546
We will raise Ertuğrul...

830
01:52:34,225 --> 01:52:37,905
together.

831
01:52:42,631 --> 01:52:47,361
He'll become a valiant
like his grandfather...

832
01:52:47,924 --> 01:52:51,924
a Ghazi.

833
01:52:51,924 --> 01:52:55,924
-Inshallah.
-Inshallah.

834
01:53:03,493 --> 01:53:08,193
You endured many troubles
since...

835
01:53:08,193 --> 01:53:12,193
you became the bey.

836
01:53:12,193 --> 01:53:16,593
You were betrayed,
you've lost comrades.

837
01:53:17,680 --> 01:53:21,680
You were wounded in your
valiant heart.

838
01:53:23,643 --> 01:53:30,843
But you endured them all at your feet.

839
01:53:34,497 --> 01:53:38,857
Your name became the hope
for the Turkish tribes...

840
01:53:38,857 --> 01:53:43,659
who cry under the scourge
of tyranny.

841
01:53:44,379 --> 01:53:48,379
Eyes are on you.

842
01:53:48,780 --> 01:53:52,780
Our prayers are with you.

843
01:53:53,382 --> 01:53:58,882
Now, Osman Bey, what do you want from us?

844
01:54:00,914 --> 01:54:05,164
Some non-Muslims from Yarhisar...

845
01:54:05,164 --> 01:54:09,814
took refuge in our tribe...

846
01:54:09,814 --> 01:54:17,354
running away from their lords.
But the heathens dare to ask them back.

847
01:54:18,596 --> 01:54:24,416
The Mongols and the Byzantines
came together.

848
01:54:24,878 --> 01:54:30,898
They want to destroy the Kayı Tribe...

849
01:54:32,130 --> 01:54:35,380
and destroy the hope of the Turks.

850
01:54:35,380 --> 01:54:38,720
It's not that easy, Osman Bey.

851
01:54:38,720 --> 01:54:44,000
We are ready for afterlife,
we drew our sword for jihad...

852
01:54:44,000 --> 01:54:50,280
even if they set fire the whole world,
we can extinguish with our heart...

853
01:54:50,280 --> 01:54:55,730
even if they collapse the blue sky down,
we can carry it with our spears.

854
01:55:01,748 --> 01:55:06,708
But my concern isn't about victory.

855
01:55:07,348 --> 01:55:11,738
Victory belongs to those who believe.

856
01:55:13,406 --> 01:55:19,376
My concern is bearing the Mongol
and Byzantine alliance alone...

857
01:55:20,423 --> 01:55:24,423
and giving many casualties.

858
01:55:25,890 --> 01:55:31,330
I want to divide the heathens...

859
01:55:31,330 --> 01:55:34,740
and destroy them separetely.

860
01:55:36,332 --> 01:55:42,722
You came here at the right time
for the right reason, Osman Bey.

861
01:55:44,685 --> 01:55:51,475
You set the foundation of your state
by protecting the refugees.

862
01:55:52,703 --> 01:55:58,023
We won't leave you alone.
Now, listen.

863
01:56:02,769 --> 01:56:06,769
İkizce? Why İkizce?

864
01:56:06,769 --> 01:56:12,409
Corpses with no graves.
A feast for the crows.

865
01:56:12,793 --> 01:56:16,793
And it will be joy for us.

866
01:56:17,099 --> 01:56:22,449
When we attack from two sides,
it's the only place Osman can run to.

867
01:56:28,181 --> 01:56:34,491
Osman Bey, this Melik
still hasn't returned.

868
01:56:34,680 --> 01:56:39,510
-Maybe he took refuge in Nikola?
-He doesn't go against his master.

869
01:56:40,676 --> 01:56:44,876
As long as we have Petros, he
won't try that.

870
01:56:44,876 --> 01:56:49,726
And he would've done that before
if he meant to.

871
01:56:51,042 --> 01:56:55,912
So, there is only one possibility.

872
01:56:55,912 --> 01:57:00,712
Nikola knows that we keep
Melik as a captive.

873
01:57:01,511 --> 01:57:05,511
And he killed him.

874
01:57:08,278 --> 01:57:12,878
-How are the alps, brother?
-Their mood is up.

875
01:57:12,878 --> 01:57:17,468
Don't worry. They all know
the importance.

876
01:57:17,468 --> 01:57:22,288
They are ready to fight and die.

877
01:57:22,288 --> 01:57:29,748
-Are they ready for victory?
-Thank Allah, no one doubts that.

878
01:57:33,059 --> 01:57:39,579
Brother! My loyal and enduring brother!

879
01:57:40,381 --> 01:57:45,021
You did everything I asked.
You were always with me.

880
01:57:45,021 --> 01:57:49,351
-I give you my blessing. Give me yours.
-What are you saying, brother?

881
01:57:49,351 --> 01:57:55,921
Of course, my blessing is yours.

882
01:58:13,806 --> 01:58:19,176
After my uncle left,
we are three brothers.

883
01:58:19,516 --> 01:58:25,916
We should be closer, we should talk.
Know each other's value.

884
01:58:29,276 --> 01:58:34,026
My brother, of course we should.

885
01:58:35,659 --> 01:58:39,659
We are each other's everything.

886
01:58:40,026 --> 01:58:44,026
The time that Allah destine us to live...

887
01:58:44,026 --> 01:58:48,026
should be spent like this, together.

888
01:58:48,489 --> 01:58:51,989
Inshallah.

889
01:58:52,492 --> 01:58:56,492
Let us survive this war,
return to the tribe.

890
01:58:56,492 --> 01:59:01,602
We can talk about our victory
and chat here.

891
01:59:02,113 --> 01:59:06,113
-My brother Savcı will be happy too.
-Inshallah.

892
01:59:06,693 --> 01:59:09,933
-Brother.
-Brother.

893
01:59:31,914 --> 01:59:35,914
-Simon?
-Get up, you lazy man!

894
01:59:35,914 --> 01:59:38,984
Is that you?

895
01:59:52,203 --> 01:59:56,643
You should call me Melik now.

896
01:59:56,907 --> 02:00:01,577
I want you to die.

897
02:00:02,315 --> 02:00:06,315
I'm dead.

898
02:00:06,315 --> 02:00:11,575
Now it's your turn, Petros.

899
02:00:11,890 --> 02:00:21,360
No! No!
No! No!

900
02:00:32,170 --> 02:00:37,110
Where are you, Simon?
Where are you? Where are you?

901
02:00:55,840 --> 02:01:00,440
Tomorrow, it's the battle day.

902
02:01:06,010 --> 02:01:10,010
It's the day to settle everything.

903
02:01:13,686 --> 02:01:20,046
I'll behead Nikola with
my sword.

904
02:01:22,151 --> 02:01:27,041
Don't worry, mother. We'll strike
the heathens and come back.

905
02:01:29,491 --> 02:01:34,071
We are destined with jihad.
You should get used to it.

906
02:01:34,592 --> 02:01:39,762
Everywhere was white, mother.

907
02:01:42,152 --> 02:01:46,992
A bird flied away from my mouth.

908
02:01:47,698 --> 02:01:52,968
It flied far away.

909
02:01:54,942 --> 02:01:58,942
It was like it was flying away
from a cage, mother.

910
02:02:00,843 --> 02:02:04,843
-It flew away.
-No!

911
02:02:11,511 --> 02:02:15,111
No! No!

912
02:02:20,110 --> 02:02:23,760
Mother, I couldn't go...

913
02:02:47,576 --> 02:02:51,576
Jihad is an obligation for the muslims...

914
02:02:52,238 --> 02:02:56,238
you can't just stay, can you?

915
02:02:56,606 --> 02:03:00,606
It is an obligation, Lena.

916
02:03:01,386 --> 02:03:07,036
It is the greatest of the obligations
for the ghazis.

917
02:03:10,940 --> 02:03:14,940
I know, you will go.

918
02:03:14,940 --> 02:03:18,940
I know, there is no other way.

919
02:03:18,940 --> 02:03:22,110
But it weights my heart, Savcı.

920
02:03:24,486 --> 02:03:29,406
When I return with victory,
it will ease.

921
02:03:30,019 --> 02:03:35,339
Don't worry, Lena.
I won't leave you alone.

922
02:03:37,146 --> 02:03:42,506
I will come bag for you
and my valiant.

923
02:03:43,443 --> 02:03:47,443
I will bring you good news.

924
02:03:51,028 --> 02:03:55,028
Is there better news than your return?

925
02:03:55,489 --> 02:04:01,309
The post of my tent,
the sultan of my heart.

926
02:04:03,304 --> 02:04:07,304
My beautiful wife who
waits in my tent.

927
02:04:14,218 --> 02:04:18,218
The reason I return
from victories.

928
02:04:18,476 --> 02:04:22,246
The star of my night.

929
02:04:22,486 --> 02:04:25,426
My gem.

930
02:04:55,961 --> 02:05:01,831
-Does my father know that you are coming?
-Sooner or later, our bey will hear.

931
02:05:01,831 --> 02:05:05,831
We are afraid that it might
be a mistake.

932
02:05:08,104 --> 02:05:12,564
The mistake is mine.
You are my alps.

933
02:05:12,564 --> 02:05:17,134
When did you see an order of mine that
doesn't fit an alp?

934
02:05:17,134 --> 02:05:21,134
In that case, my life
and blood is yours, don't you know?

935
02:05:25,411 --> 02:05:28,771
Come on.

936
02:05:31,839 --> 02:05:35,839
My alps! Say what you will now.

937
02:05:35,839 --> 02:05:39,839
We'll get in war with Osman Bey now.

938
02:05:39,839 --> 02:05:43,839
If you don't want, return.

939
02:05:44,925 --> 02:05:50,035
But know that...

940
02:05:50,823 --> 02:05:55,283
even if I'm alone, I will stand
with Osman Bey until my last breath!

941
02:06:04,122 --> 02:06:08,372
Malhun Hatun, Osman Bey is coming
with his alps.

942
02:06:08,372 --> 02:06:15,142
Now, I'm asking for the last time,
is there anyone who wants to return?

943
02:06:39,117 --> 02:06:44,077
-What is it, Malhun Hatun?
-We heard that you are going for jihad.

944
02:06:44,690 --> 02:06:49,130
We want to join you in your cause.

945
02:06:55,023 --> 02:07:00,993
The fate of these land that you came
to, depends on this battle.

946
02:07:01,225 --> 02:07:06,235
Your alps are eager for battle,
I see that.

947
02:07:06,957 --> 02:07:11,907
But they are concerned
about their bey.

948
02:07:12,457 --> 02:07:19,007
My alps are ready to fight in your cause
for Allah.

949
02:07:19,867 --> 02:07:23,867
The honor of fighting alongside you
is on my tribe...

950
02:07:23,867 --> 02:07:27,867
and my bey's fury is on me.

951
02:07:31,016 --> 02:07:35,016
I sacrifice my life for this cause,
Osman Bey.

952
02:07:35,016 --> 02:07:39,366
It's an honor to fight alongside you and
this valiant woman, Osman Bey.

953
02:07:47,006 --> 02:07:51,846
Malhun Hatun's valiant alps...

954
02:07:51,846 --> 02:07:57,796
know that these lands that you came after
running away from the Mongols...

955
02:07:58,390 --> 02:08:02,390
is the last haven of the Turks.

956
02:08:02,696 --> 02:08:06,696
We will strike the last and the strongest
blow...

957
02:08:06,696 --> 02:08:10,696
all together, against
all the mischiefs...

958
02:08:10,696 --> 02:08:14,696
of the unhonorable enemy!

959
02:08:14,696 --> 02:08:19,706
In the path that our ancestors opened...

960
02:08:19,706 --> 02:08:23,671
you will cause the foundation of
a great state...

961
02:08:23,671 --> 02:08:29,621
with your lives, blood and
Allah's help.

962
02:08:30,461 --> 02:08:37,001
We won't bow down to either Mongols
or the Byzantines!

963
02:08:37,394 --> 02:08:42,244
Neither their armies nor their
twisted plans...

964
02:08:42,244 --> 02:08:47,614
will stop our unity!

965
02:08:48,670 --> 02:08:52,670
Bravery takes us to victory...

966
02:08:52,670 --> 02:08:56,310
cowardice takes us to defeat!

967
02:08:56,310 --> 02:09:00,670
The power that we need
is in...

968
02:09:00,670 --> 02:09:04,670
the noble blood we carry
in our veins...

969
02:09:04,670 --> 02:09:09,570
and in our faith.

970
02:09:11,051 --> 02:09:15,051
Here, I see such an unbreakable
will...

971
02:09:15,051 --> 02:09:19,051
men and women all together!

972
02:09:20,519 --> 02:09:24,519
I thank my holy Allah!

973
02:09:24,519 --> 02:09:28,519
But don't you ever forget!

974
02:09:28,604 --> 02:09:35,464
Allah... Allah is with us!

975
02:09:39,159 --> 02:09:56,932
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

976
02:09:57,289 --> 02:10:03,707
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com